  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following statements are true?<br />(A) The subsidiary quantum number $l$ describes the shape of the orbital occupied by the electron.<br />(B) <br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/YapBBT1J9mCNfTz6f9-pD-4tZnHtmVS1n1qk0omuCzg.original.fullsize.png\"/><br />is the boundary surface diagram of the $2 p_x$ orbital.<br />(C) The + and - signs in the wave function of the $2 \\mathrm{p}_{\\mathrm{x}}$ orbital refer to charge.<br />(D) The wave function of $2 p_x$ orbital is zero everywhere in the xy plane.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "PqyI1",
      "text": "(B) and (D) only",
