  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "(A) Azimuthal quantum number $(\\ell)$ indicates the shape of orbital occupied by the electron<br />(B) <br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/z1LGMicFIXLGbktMd7mK5sXD-rpakJ8Vz3ehYRAEZuk.original.fullsize.png\"/><br />$\\mathrm{p}_{\\mathrm{x}}$ orbital<br />(C) The + and - sign in the wave function of $2 p_x$ orbital refer to the sign (Phase) of the wave function, not the charge<br />(D) The wave function of $2 p_x$ orbital will be zero in yz plane (Nodal plane).",
    "image": null
  },
